# WHAT A CLI DEPLOY MUST NOT UPLOAD — and why this file has to exist at all.
#
# THE VERCEL CLI DOES NOT READ .gitignore. It reads THIS file, plus a short built-in list
# (node_modules, .git, .next, .vercel, .env*). Everything else in the working tree is
# uploaded, whether or not git has ever heard of it. That is the opposite of the Git
# integration's behaviour, where only committed files are ever sent — and srsly deploys from
# the CLI (see the note in CLAUDE.md), so the safe-by-default half does not apply here.
#
# WITHOUT THIS FILE A DEPLOY UPLOADED 2.2 GB ACROSS 11,588 FILES. Measured, 2026-10-04:
#
#   measurements/   1.9 GB   6,476 files   readability-sweep dumps
#   .next-agent/    244 MB     137 files   build output for the agent dev server
#
# `measurements/` is the worst of it and it GROWS ~300 MB EVERY SWEEP DAY, because each run
# keeps a whole Chrome profile — 1,274 PNGs, 157 tflite models, several of them 35 MB each.
# The same directory already had to be added to eslint.config.mjs for the same reason
# ("lint went from clean to 796 problems across six vendor files nobody wrote"), which is the
# tell: a tool that walks the project tree will find this directory unless it is told not to.
#
# .next-agent is NOT covered by the built-in `.next` exclusion — that is an exact name, not a
# prefix — which is exactly the trap eslint.config.mjs already records about naming build dirs
# one at a time. Globs here for the same reason.

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next*/
out/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Measurement dumps: provider quota to produce, never part of a deployment ──
measurements/

# ── Secrets, belt and braces ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The CLI already excludes these. Listed anyway: a credential uploaded once is a credential
# leaked, and this repository has had to rotate a key before.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vercel

# ── Local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.DS_Store
